Z||000001||Pretender||08-15-99||01:21 AM||||I've stressed this mod to many but few have believed. i installed the ADS chip and the power pully from the fiero store and i gained 4 tenths in the 1/4 mile!...it's super easy to install. It re-calibrates the air fuel mixture and changes the shiftpoints, it also requires to run without a cat. but i have a way around the emisions tests(pa doesn't check yet) It was worth the money to me. L8r.
Z||000002||terryk||08-15-99||01:09 PM||||This surprises me since the Fiero is run rich in fuel. Leaning them out some tends to make them a bit faster. But .4s in the quarter translate to some significant HP which really isn't in the engine in the first place. Look at the O2 at WOT. What does it read?<p>Not a flame, just a surprise.<p>Not sure what you mean by shift points, since neither the manual or auto is ECM controlled. Maybe they moved the shift light points.
Z||000003||mwbackus||08-15-99||02:37 PM||||I believe that the performance enhancement provided by these chips is obtained not only by an alteration of the fuel map, but also a more agressive timing curve (hence the need for premium fuel to avoid ping,etc.).  I would also submit that the underdrive pulley probably had more effect on actual performance than the chip.  Myself, the only chip I would consider using is the thermomaster from Hypertech.  The themomaster chip, used with a low temp stat and fan switch, can provide significant performance benefits. This is based on controlled dyno test runs conducted on the various chips by Road & Track magazine, although I cannot recall the exact issue it was presented in.<p>Mike
Z||000004||terryk||08-15-99||03:21 PM||||I'd be curious to get a binary of the chip to see what was changed. Might be very telling.
